          ],
          "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.894,
            0.12,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": "194"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "2. When the plant is kept inverted, the root bends and grows downwards. Also, the shoot bends and grows upwards."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.129,
            0.883,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "3. When the plant gets sunlight only from one direction, the shoot grows in the direction of light while the root continues to grow downwards."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.196,
            0.883,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "After conducting Activity 10.3, we can conclude that shoots of plants grow upward and exhibit movement towards sunlight but roots of plants grow downwards."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.282,
            0.372,
            0.303
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Know a scientist"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.335,
            0.711,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "**Jagadish Chandra Bose** (1858–1937) was an Indian scientist who did some fascinating experiments with plants. He built a machine called a crescograph to record how plants respond to stimuli like light, heat, electricity and gravity. With this machine, he could measure how fast plants grow. He also showed that plants can sense and respond to stimuli."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.714,
            0.305,
            0.872,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.493,
            0.583,
            0.519
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "10.4 Life Cycle of a Plant"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.529,
            0.883,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "We have learnt about conditions required for germination and how plants grow and exhibit movement. Let us now explore the changes a plant undergoes in its whole life."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.603,
            0.559,
            0.625
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 10.4: Let us explore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.636,
            0.882,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": " Plant a bean seed and provide suitable conditions for its growth. Observe regularly for three months."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.686,
            0.883,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": " Record your observations in Table 10.4 as and when changes become visible."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.735,
            0.883,
            0.779
          ],
          "content": "Note the date when any change is observed. Record answers for the following questions—"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.784,
            0.883,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": " How long does it take for any change to occur? Make sketches of various changes that you observe in Table 10.4."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.855,
            0.862,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": " After how many days does the first flower appear?"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
